import{_ as o,o as n,c as t,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 875 | Transcended Ones and Economy | More-Work-More-Pay Transcended-One Allocation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 875 | Transcended Ones and Economy | More-Work-More-Pay Transcended-One Allocation","no":875,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Economy","More-Work-More-Pay","Allocation","Civilizational Weight"],"related":["06-More-Work-More-Pay Distribution Principle","22-Resource Allocation Household-Responsibility Mechanism","724-Perpetual Construction More-Work-More-Pay Distribution","727-Perpetual Construction Civilizational-Weight Incentive"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0875_模块4-超脱者与经济-多劳多得的超脱者分配.md","filePath":"en/0875_模块4-超脱者与经济-多劳多得的超脱者分配.md"}'),i={name:"en/0875_模块4-超脱者与经济-多劳多得的超脱者分配.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,h){return n(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-875-transcended-ones-and-economy-more-work-more-pay-transcended-one-allocation" tabindex="-1">Entry 875 | Transcended Ones and Economy | More-Work-More-Pay Transcended-One Allocation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-875-transcended-ones-and-economy-more-work-more-pay-transcended-one-allocation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 875 | Transcended Ones and Economy | More-Work-More-Pay Transcended-One Allocation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 06, 22, 724, 727</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-transcended-one-is-not-a-retired-cadre-—-how-much-he-takes-depends-entirely-on-how-much-he-did" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the transcended one is not a retired cadre — how much he takes depends entirely on how much he did <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-transcended-one-is-not-a-retired-cadre-—-how-much-he-takes-depends-entirely-on-how-much-he-did" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the transcended one is not a retired cadre — how much he takes depends entirely on how much he did&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s allocation to the strong is &quot;status allocation&quot;: what realm you are in, what treatment you get. The Great Emperor lives in an imperial palace, uses immortal artifacts, receives Myriad Ranks&#39; offerings — not because he did much work, but because he is strongest. Heng Yuan Zhou reverses this: <strong>how much the transcended one takes depends not on how strong he is, but on how much work he did.</strong> This is more-work-more-pay&#39;s concrete execution on the transcended one. This entry explains the transcended one&#39;s allocation mechanism.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the anti-predation axiom negates the &quot;strong take all&quot; allocation logic; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires allocation be fair and open; the collective ascension axiom requires allocation incentivize Myriad-Rank co-building; the causal self-discipline axiom requires allocation be traceable throughout; the law-first axiom requires allocation laws be self-consistent, not manipulated by personal ties; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-why-the-old-world-s-allocation-is-inevitable-unfair" tabindex="-1">I. Why the Old World&#39;s Allocation Is Inevitable Unfair <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-why-the-old-world-s-allocation-is-inevitable-unfair" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Why the Old World&#39;s Allocation Is Inevitable Unfair&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s allocation rules look also very &quot;reasonable&quot;:</p><ul><li>Sect-competition winner takes the first-place prize;</li><li>Secret-realm exploration first-come-first-served;</li><li>Higher cultivation gets more resources.</li></ul><p>But these rules&#39; premise is &quot;fair starting point&quot; — and the starting point is never fair. Great-sect children have the best resources from childhood; scattered cultivators start behind the starting line from birth. So-called &quot;fair competition&quot; only wraps starting-point unfairness in rules.</p><p>A deeper problem is: <strong>allocation decoupled from contribution.</strong> A Great Emperor may have sat in the imperial palace for a hundred thousand years, doing nothing, but his offerings do not decrease a bit. A bottom-level cultivator may have worked in a workshop a lifetime, retiring with nothing. This is not more-work-more-pay; this is more-grab-more-pay.</p><h2 id="ii-heng-yuan-zhou-s-allocation-formula" tabindex="-1">II. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Allocation Formula <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-heng-yuan-zhou-s-allocation-formula" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Allocation Formula&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s allocation formula for the transcended one is very simple:</p><p><strong>Receipt = post-contribution score × increment-development score × civilizational-weight coefficient × supervision score</strong></p><p>The four variables&#39; meanings:</p><ol><li><strong>Post-contribution score</strong>: quantified score of the transcended one&#39;s completing legal post duties (law maintenance, Myriad-Rank guidance, cross-plane construction, etc.);</li><li><strong>Increment-development score</strong>: quantified score of the transcended one opening new resources, new planes, new laws;</li><li><strong>Civilizational-weight coefficient</strong>: comprehensively calculated from the transcended one&#39;s historical contributions, post difficulty, Myriad-Rank evaluation;</li><li><strong>Supervision score</strong>: Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s compliance score; deductions for violations, bonuses for cooperation.</li></ol><p>This formula&#39;s core is: <strong>no look at birth, lineage, or clan; only look at contribution.</strong> Do more → take more; do less → take less; do nothing → demote.</p><h2 id="iii-several-allocation-hard-rules" tabindex="-1">III. Several Allocation Hard Rules <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-several-allocation-hard-rules" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Several Allocation Hard Rules&quot;">​</a></h2><p>More-work-more-pay is not empty words; it has several hard rules:</p><ul><li><strong>No ceiling, but a protected floor</strong>: take as much as contribution warrants; no &quot;transcended-one salary ceiling&quot;; but if post assessment is unqualified, the floor lowers until transcended-one qualification is revoked;</li><li><strong>Stock does not participate in allocation</strong>: the transcended one may not allocate existing stock — his receipt must come from increment development. This ensures he does not compete with Myriad Ranks over stock;</li><li><strong>Allocation public</strong>: every transcended one&#39;s allocation detail is public network-wide through the Selfless Dao; Myriad Ranks may query;</li><li><strong>Myriad-Rank evaluation counted</strong>: the allocation formula includes Myriad-Rank satisfaction score; not &quot;self-work-self-evaluate&quot;;</li><li><strong>Allocation tied to cultivation resources</strong>: the transcended one&#39;s cultivation resources are not &quot;free supply,&quot; but disbursed from allocation — the more he does, the more cultivation resources.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-allocation-differences-between-transcended-ones" tabindex="-1">IV. Allocation Differences Between Transcended Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-allocation-differences-between-transcended-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Allocation Differences Between Transcended Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>More-work-more-pay means allocation differences between transcended ones — this is not inequality, this is reasonable incentive:</p><ul><li>A transcended one who opened a new cosmos takes far more than one who only does routine maintenance on old planes;</li><li>A transcended one who trained ten new transcended ones takes more than one who did not teach a single disciple;</li><li>A transcended one who stepped forward in crisis and protected Myriad Ranks takes more than one who usually &quot;slacks off.&quot;</li></ul><p>The difference&#39;s purpose is not to create classes, but <strong>incentivize behavior</strong>: you want more? Then do more work, open more, teach more. Not go grab, monopolize, or run small circles.</p><p>The allocation formula&#39;s transparency is critical. If how much the transcended one takes is not public, Myriad Ranks will suspect — &quot;is he embezzling?&quot; &quot;is he favoring someone?&quot; Public allocation details turn suspicion into data, turn data into trust. Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision ensures data is not falsified; Selfless Dao network-wide opening ensures everyone can query. When allocation is transparent, Myriad Ranks will not internally wear down over &quot;unfairness.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: allocation tied to contribution, eliminating the energy waste of &quot;holding a post without working&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: allocation comes from increment not stock; the transcended one need not prey on Myriad Ranks to support himself</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo&#39;s allocation is grace system — he gives whomever he gives, the standard in his heart; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s allocation is formula system — four variables all public, the standard in Myriad Ranks&#39; hands</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the allocation formula treats transcended ones from five Myriad-Rank lineages equally</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the allocation formula and every transcended one&#39;s allocation detail open network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>More-work-more-pay&#39;s execution on the transcended one turns &quot;status allocation&quot; into &quot;contribution allocation.&quot; How much the transcended one takes depends not on how strong he is, but on how much work he did; not on who he is, but on how much increment he created. Do more → take more; do nothing → demote. This is not coldness; this is fairness — true Myriad-Rank republicanism means even the strongest must work for his own keep. This is the orthodox definition of transcended-one allocation.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/06-多劳多得分配原理.html">Entry 06 · More-Work-More-Pay Distribution Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">Entry 22 · Resource Allocation Household-Responsibility Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/724_模块4-永动建设的多劳多得分配.html">Entry 724 · Perpetual Construction More-Work-More-Pay Distribution</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/727_模块4-永动建设的文明权重激励.html">Entry 727 · Perpetual Construction Civilizational-Weight Incentive</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const p=o(i,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
